I **did not complete the requested remediation**. The candidate remains partial; the publication finding is still open, so the work should not be treated as accepted.

I verified all 20 archived source hashes against `remediation-source-seed.json` before editing and preserved the archived candidate and inherited fixes/tests. Production text requests now use controlled family, position-list, entity, and whitespace scans. Outline generation has an offset-aware entry point, and production geometry errors carry the authored run offset. I also updated the README and work-order reports to record the open findings.

**Publication remains vulnerable:** `StylePublisher::publish` still receives `CustomGeometry` with the admission token and can append geometry itself. The existing metadata checks can still accept equal-sized replacement geometry. This appears fixable within the media crate; I made no claim of a shared Scene contract gap.

Verification passed:

- `CARGO_HOME="$PWD/.cache/cargo" cargo +stable check -p vexel-svg-media --locked --offline`
- `CARGO_HOME="$PWD/.cache/cargo" cargo +stable test -p vexel-svg-media --locked --offline` — 60 integration tests passed
- `python3 scripts/wo_validate.py WO-RUST-SVG-MEDIA-01 --ready`

The requested interruption-inside-scan rollback/reuse tests and late outline failure/offset and growth-limit tests are still missing. The reports mark those gaps and the publication finding as open.
